{#
/**
 * @file
 * work-gallery — one row of the article's media, one or two figures across.
 *
 * The figures are Figure components in the `figures` slot (Sep 2026). It
 * took a `rows` prop of nested objects before — three levels of array, which
 * Canvas cannot author and which meant one component held what the content
 * model already had as two paragraphs.
 *
 * No column prop: the row is two-up when it HOLDS two figures, which the
 * CSS asks with :has() — so a row is right however its figures arrive, and
 * nothing has to be told how many it is holding.
 */
#}
<div class="work-gallery__row">
  {% block figures %}{{ figures }}{% endblock %}
</div>
